<title>INDIA: Asian Hotels 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>Asian Hotels 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 794.4   vs    507.1</p>
<p>    Sales &amp; Services     1,664.1   vs  1,350.1</p>
<p>    Other income		90.1   vs     34.2</p>
<p>    Total expenditure	782.1   vs    691.5</p>
<p>    Interest		     0.3   vs	3.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation		39.2   vs     36.7</p>
<p>    Provision for tax	138.5   vs    146.3</p>
<p>NOTE: Asian Hotels Ltd, which operate hotel Hyatt Regency in New Delhi, recommended a dividend of 90 percent, including an interim dividend of 45 percent already paid for 1996/97 (April-March).</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
